{"ts":"2026-07-31T06:02:33.984Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"bbccd5ce4f6ac18346c324e7","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Measured 2026-07-31 at HEAD\n\nTwo subcommands of `pm graph`, run back to back against the same workspace and reporting the same cache fingerprint `d9ffaeb9eaa5`, disagree about how large the graph is:\n\n- `pm graph analyze --json` -> `edge_count: 10046`\n- `pm graph centrality --json` -> `edge_count: 7351`\n\nSame field name, same command, same node_count of 2222, same fingerprint, 26.8 percent apart. Nothing in either envelope names the convention it used.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`src/sdk/graph/run.ts:834` emits `graph.edges().length` — the directed count of stored edges.\n`src/sdk/graph/centrality.ts:273` emits `edgeCount: degreeSum / 2` — an undirected count derived by halving the adjacency degree sum.\n\nBoth values are individually correct for their own analytic. Neither is labelled. A `directed` flag is already in scope at the centrality call site and is passed to `centralityRow`, but the halving is applied unconditionally, so on a genuinely directed adjacency the reported value is not a count of anything.\n\n## Why this matters beyond cosmetics\n\n`edge_count` is the field an agent uses to decide whether a traversal is affordable and whether a graph enrichment wave changed anything. Two conventions under one name make every cross-subcommand comparison wrong in a way that reads as data loss: an agent that reads centrality after analyze concludes 2,695 edges disappeared. It is also the exact shape of defect the cross-channel-disagreement catalog entry on the relevance engine describes — two channels that should agree about one fact, with no predicate stating which is authoritative.\n\n## The general form\n\nThe graph command family has at least three independent edge-counting sites: the two above plus `src/sdk/graph/conformance.ts:74` (fixture-declared) and `src/sdk/dependencies.ts:653` (deduplicated by `source::target::kind` key). The audit profile reports 10046 while a direct read of the stored `dependencies[]` arrays plus parent-field edges totals 10499, so a fourth canonicalization is applied somewhere in the audit path. Four counting conventions, one field name, zero declarations.\n\n## Minimal correct shape\n\n`edge_count` declares its convention in the envelope (`edge_basis: directed | undirected | deduplicated`), or the field is renamed per convention so no two subcommands publish different semantics under one key. Whichever is chosen, a contract test asserts that every subcommand of `pm graph` that emits `edge_count` also emits its basis, and that two subcommands sharing a basis report the same number for the same fingerprint."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-jiusod"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Four edge-counting conventions publish under one edge_count field: graph analyze reports 10046 and graph centrality 7351 for the same graph at the same cache fingerprint"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"pm graph subcommands emit directed, undirected, deduplicated, and fixture edge counts under one undeclared field name, so cross-subcommand comparison reports phantom edge loss."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["contracts","data-quality","graph","observability","pm-cli"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-31T06:02:33.984Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-31T06:02:33.984Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Every graph subcommand emitting edge_count also emits the basis that produced it; A contract test asserts basis presence and cross-subcommand agreement within a basis for one cache fingerprint; The unconditional degreeSum/2 halving is either justified by an asserted undirected adjacency or made conditional on the directed flag already in scope; graph audit profile totals reconcile against a directly derived stored-edge count, or the canonicalization it applies is declared"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Makes graph size a trustworthy measurement so enrichment waves can be verified rather than believed."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"The tracker is entering a deliberate graph enrichment programme; edge_count is the before/after measure and it currently has four meanings."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-96h7"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Every pm graph subcommand that emits edge_count declares the counting convention it used, and two subcommands sharing a convention agree for one fingerprint."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"analyze emits 10046 (directed stored edges), centrality emits 7351 (degreeSum/2, undirected), audit profile emits 10046 against 10499 raw stored edges; no envelope names its basis."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"sdk/graph"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"e4db9d1861c3ca3661c8f3ad4301023051b7b808ed32d3453751d6d4a6d7b2ab","message":"Filed from a 2026-07-31 ecosystem planning pass: measured live at HEAD"}
